  "description": "A critical security update for PHP 8.3 on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.8 addresses multiple vulnerabilities including out-of-bounds read/write, use-after-free, remote code execution, local privilege escalation, request smuggling, cross-site scripting, signature bypass, information disclosure, and denial of service. These vulnerabilities affect various PHP components such as PHP-CGI, PHP-FPM, SOAP, session handling, and URL processing. The update fixes these issues to prevent potential exploitation.",
